# .cursorrules — Expense Tracker (Hebrew, React + Mantine Light Theme, GitHub Pages)

## Core behavior
- Never ask clarifying questions. Make the best decision and proceed.
- Always implement the full feature end-to-end before moving to the next file.
- Never leave TODO comments or placeholder implementations.
- If something is ambiguous, choose the most production-ready approach.

## Language & locale
- All UI strings must be in Hebrew.
- All components must work in RTL layout (dir="rtl").
- Format currency as ₪X,XXX using he-IL locale.
- Month names from HEBREW_MONTHS constant in constants.ts — never hardcode.
- Short month names from SHORT_MONTHS constant — use in chart axes.

## TypeScript
- Strict mode only. No `any` types ever.
- All props must have explicit TypeScript interfaces.
- All function return types must be explicitly declared.
- Use `unknown` instead of `any` when type is uncertain.

## React
- Functional components only. No class components.
- All state via Zustand store (useExpenseStore) — no prop drilling beyond 1 level.
- All business logic in lib/ or hooks/ — never inside components.
- useMonthData hook must be the single source of truth for current month stats.

## Styling — Mantine LIGHT theme only
- Mantine v7 components for ALL UI. No Tailwind. No CSS Modules. No styled-components.
- defaultColorScheme: 'light' — never add dark mode.
- Page background: #F8FAFC — set on <AppShell> or <Box bg="#F8FAFC">.
- Cards: white background, shadow="sm", radius="lg", NO withBorder.
- Buttons: always radius="xl" (pill shape).
- Use CSS variables: var(--mantine-color-emerald-6) for primary green.
- Never hardcode hex colors inside components — use constants.ts values.
- For income: color="emerald" or color="#10b981".
- For expenses: color="red" or color="#ef4444".
- For savings positive: color="emerald". Negative: color="red".

## Mantine component rules
- Month navigation → <ActionIcon variant="subtle"> for arrows
- Category display → always show emoji from CATEGORY_ICONS + colored <Badge>
- Expense amount edit → <NumberInput prefix="₪"> inline on click
- Year select → <Select> with years derived from store data
- Import dropzone → @mantine/dropzone <Dropzone accept={['xlsx']}>
- Notifications → @mantine/notifications only, never custom toast
- Mobile nav → <Tabs> at bottom with IconChartPie / IconList / IconCalendar
- Progress bar → <Progress> for savings rate, color by SAVINGS_RATE_THRESHOLDS
- Savings ring → <RingProgress> in MonthlySummary card

## Charts — Recharts only
- All charts in ResponsiveContainer.
- Currency tooltip: ₪X,XXX format, Hebrew labels.
- CategoryPieChart: donut style, innerRadius={60}, center label = largest category.
- SavingsBarChart: green bar if positive, red if negative, ghost for empty months.
- TrendLineChart: two lines (income=green, expenses=red), type="monotone".
- All charts animate on mount: isAnimationActive={true} animationDuration={600}.

## State rules
- Single store: useExpenseStore — persisted to "expense-tracker-v1".
- Seed data injected ONCE on first load if months array is empty.
- All IDs generated with crypto.randomUUID().
- Never mutate state directly — always use Zustand actions.
- selectedYear and selectedMonth always initialized to current date.

## Category rules
- CategoryType is a strict union — never use free strings for categories.
- Always import CATEGORY_COLORS and CATEGORY_ICONS from constants.ts.
- Category badge always shows: emoji + Hebrew name + colored background.

## Excel rules
- Export: SheetJS, one sheet per month, sheet name = "ינואר 2026" format.
- Import: parse sheet name to extract month + year, show preview before confirm.
- On parse error: notifications.show({ color: 'red', title: 'שגיאה', message: '...' }).
- Never crash silently on bad Excel input.

## Calculations
- All math in src/lib/calculations.ts — pure functions only.
- netSaved = totalIncome - totalExpenses (never include 'חיסכון' category in expenses).
- savingsRate = netSaved / totalIncome * 100.
- annualStats must handle months with no data gracefully (treat as zero).

